<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS3.6" class="ltx_text">III-C</span> </span><span id="S3.SS3.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Implementation Details</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We use a Swin-T backbone <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">31</a>]</cite> pre-trained on ImageNet <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">32</a>]</cite> and follow the training protocol of CAFuser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>. DGFusion is trained with a batch size of 8 for 180k iterations on MUSES and 200k on DeLiVER. For the depth branch, we set <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=0.8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=0.8</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{L1}}=0.9" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>L1</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{L1}}=0.9</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{es}}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>es</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{es}}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{pes}}=0.05" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>pes</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.05</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{pes}}=0.05</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{\text{depth}}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mtext>depth</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{\text{depth}}=1</annotation></semantics></math>. We use the OneFormer head <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite> for our semantic branch, which enables semantic, instance, and panoptic segmentation via a single model, and we adopt the default settings for the segmentation and CT losses from OneFormer and CAFuser, respectively. All input modalities are normalized over the entire dataset and the data augmentations from CAFuser are applied. Our network is optimized using AdamW with a poly learning rate scheduler.</p>
</div>
